    "summary": "High‑energy set with stellar Alligator>Other One and tight Not Fade Away",
    "blurb": "The July 10, 1970 Fillmore East show bursts out of the gate with a crisp Cold Rain And Snow and rolls into an inspired Alligator → The Other One suite that stays in the pocket all night. Jerry’s tone is extraordinary while Bob’s vocal‑guitar blend shines on the Not Fade Away closer. Though captured on a lo‑fi audience tape, the recording retains enough clarity to feel like you’re right there in the hall.",
    "review": "On July 10, 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead were firing on all cylinders. The first set opens with a bright, rolling Cold Rain And Snow that immediately sets a high‑energy tone. From there the band launches into an Alligator that morphs seamlessly into The Other One, a stretch highlighted by Jerry’s soaring lead tones and his “mind‑meld” interplay with Bob during the Not Fade Away closer. Attics Of My Life follows, offering a lyrical respite before the band dives back into the electric jam corridor with Cryptical Envelopment, Cosmic Charlie, and a double dose of Good Lovin’ that bridges two drum solos. The encore caps the night with a rousing Not Fade Away that showcases Bob’s vocal‑guitar blend and Jerry’s melodic phrasing. While the sole surviving recording is an audience tape—cloudy, low‑end, with occasional crowd bleed—it remains surprisingly listenable for 1970 standards and captures the band’s palpable excitement throughout the evening.",
